{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage","id":1550508,"title":"I always felt the Hollow Ones should have been the protagonists of Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-30T04:31:42-07:00","id":1550508,"title":"I always felt the Hollow Ones should have been the protagonists of Mage","content":"I have an excessive love of the Hollow Ones. Maybe it's because I was always a Goth at heart but lacked the fashion sense. However, I feel like the Hollow Ones were meant for a bigger role in the Mage: The Ascension metaplot but sort of got shoved to the side. I was always influenced on this by the OUTCASTS supplement that portrayed them as a uniquely adapted Craft that wanted to survive in the post-modern magical world of the WOD without the Ascension War clouding their judgement (but willing to defend themselves).<br /> <br /> <img width=\"232\" height=\"300\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cf.geekdo-images.com/3Ufw64MzlFPggrXBelnoNw__itemrep/img/2NhMRJnrcoxlQAfWaVJICdI5iZU=/fit-in/246x300/filters:strip_icc()/pic513931.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cf.geekdo-images.com/3Ufw64MzlFPggrXBelnoNw__itemrep/img/2NhMRJnrcoxlQAfWaVJICdI5iZU=/fit-in/246x300/filters:strip_icc()/pic513931.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cf.geekdo-images.com/3Ufw64MzlFPggrXBelnoNw__itemrep/img/2NhMRJnrcoxlQAfWaVJICdI5iZU=/fit-in/246x300/filters:strip_icc()/pic513931.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I think this is also because they were heavily promoted as the &quot;Orphan&quot; faction. They've been awakened by the world around them and not really weighed down by the excessive tradition and naval gazing of the Traditions. Sort of like how House Thig was later depicted. In a very real way, their DIY take on magic was the best sort of progress that Magick as a whole was needing as they could combine magick, occult, and technology in interfaith smoothies that didn't contradict one another.<br /> <br /> And they just...didn't.<br /> <br /> They didn't become reformers, Anarchs, or major players. They didn't rise to the occassion in Revised.<br /> <br /> They just sort of ...were there.<br /> <br /> The Alliance was a good idea but I don't think the Hollow Ones would ever join either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T05:56:44-07:00","id":1550510,"title":"","content":"I agree with all of your points. I really like the Hollow Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 04-30-2025, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T06:26:52-07:00","id":1550512,"title":"","content":"No battle plan survives contact with the enemy or in this case the marketplace. Given the cultural/political mood White Wolf and Onyx Path seems to have maintained since the 1990s the Hollow Ones were destined to be the stars. Some of this still lingers around. <br /> <br /> The Disparates are brought together by the Hollow Ones to fight the &quot;Whitemare.&quot; Which might charm the Hollow Ones but where were they getting the leadership skills?<br /> <br /> Victorian Mage made the Hollow Ones anarchists throwing bombs at the Hermetics, again meant to be the stars. But as before it went nowhere.<br /> <br /> The other trads are just to much fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T12:32:33-07:00","id":1550520,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is perhaps a structural one. The focus of the metaplot became the overthrow of the Traditions' corrupt old-guard, which is a much easier thing to approach if you're actually playing as members of those Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T12:54:38-07:00","id":1550523,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is simply that Mage isn't a punk setting, Vampire is.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but I don't get in any edition any reason for the Hollow Ones to be the protagonists.<br /> <br /> That's not to say they don't have a place in it. I'm actually a fan of them, and I know many others.<br /> <br /> But Mage is about so many other things, and many of them are about exploring your beliefs and your will to enact those beliefs on the world.<br /> <br /> And the Hollow Ones are about not believing so strongly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T14:10:40-07:00","id":1550525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550523#post1550523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Hollow Ones are about not believing so strongly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take the view the Hollow Ones are the people who understand that beliefs don't have to be contradictory or that killing over them makes them more valid. If science and magic can be combined by a Hollow One doing a spell on a labtop or using pencillian with your magic potion then what ARE the Traditions and Union fighting over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T14:38:47-07:00","id":1550527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550525#post1550525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take the view the Hollow Ones are the people who understand that beliefs don't have to be contradictory or that killing over them makes them more valid. If science and magic can be combined by a Hollow One doing a spell on a labtop or using pencillian with your magic potion then what ARE the Traditions and Union fighting over?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hollow Ones are about not assuming an overarching principle or belief for your Magic. They don't believe in any <i><b>universal theory</b></i> for Reality.<br /> <br /> It's not that everything is true, but that <b>The Truth<sup>TM</sup> </b>doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> And yes, that's a valid point, hence they're in the game. It doesn't makes them the protagonists, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T14:50:19-07:00","id":1550608,"title":"","content":"Personally i dont use them at all. Any non tradition and nontechnocracy mage is just fresh and ready to be adopted or killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T16:31:55-07:00","id":1550611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550608#post1550608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i dont use them at all. Any non tradition and nontechnocracy mage is just fresh and ready to be adopted or killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they will always exist because the more power blocks squeeze, the more enemies they will make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T05:12:38-07:00","id":1550620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why they will always exist because the more power blocks squeeze, the more enemies they will make. </div> </div> </div>To return to your original question, I think the problem is that that's a narrative <i>Ascension</i> has just never really fleshed out. <i>Outcasts</i> really wants to equivocate between the Traditions and the Technocracy, but when you actually get down to the details, it just doesn't work. Their criticisms of the Traditions are pretty vague and contradictory, and when they actually discuss the individual traditions, they're pretty chill with most of them. Even with the Hermetics, the criticism is that they're kinda rude. Like, narratively <i>Outcasts</i> (and honestly the Disparates of M20 suffer a similar issue) needs the Traditions to be this overweening authority that the Hollow Ones and Orphans can push back against, but they just aren't and the line was never willing to make them such a force so it just kinda falls flat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-03T07:30:38-07:00","id":1550625,"title":"","content":"M20 is the first point in the line where the premise of this thread has significant support \u2014 though in supporting it, it abandons the Hollow Ones as outcasts. Instead, Orphans are given more support. So much so that in <b>Mage Made Easy</b> (the STV book that Brucato used to outline his vision for what he would have done for a fourth edition if it wasn't going to be an Anniversary Edition celebrating what had come before), the <i>default</i> player characters are independent mages: instead of choosing a Tradition (or Convention or Craft), you choose an Approach \u2014 and <i>if</i> you still want to be aligned with one of the game's existing factions, each Approach suggests several for you to choose from. In M20, Focus broadly covers the same ground as MME's Approaches. <br /> <br /> So you no longer have Paradigm and Practice being gatekept behind factions, and independent mages are no longer being presented as redheaded stepchildren or black sheep. This is as opposed to, say, 1e; back then, someone asked about the fact that Orphans didn't get an Affinity Sphere, and the developer's response amounted to &quot;sucks to be them.&quot; That's why I've said before that the Hollow Ones and the Orphans weren't the heroes of the early editions, but <i>can</i> be the heroes of M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T05:32:15-07:00","id":1550656,"title":"","content":"Even while M20 made Orphans a more interesting option than they were before, I find it a hard sell to say they're <i>the</i> heroes, or protagonists, of the game. If anything, M20 made it easier to have <i><b>any</b></i> faction or option as a protagonist, but none is particularly better at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T06:38:10-07:00","id":1550659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550656#post1550656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even while M20 made Orphans a more interesting option than they were before, I find it a hard sell to say they're <i>the</i> heroes, or protagonists, of the game. If anything, M20 made it easier to have <i><b>any</b></i> faction or option as a protagonist, but none is particularly better at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that most factions are fairly close in protagonist potential. The Trads seem to have an edge, but that doesn't really seem intentional. Still, there are hints and clues from the 1st ed onward that the authors wanted us all to see the Hollow Ones as the especially KWEL kids. <br /> <br /> Just because they didn't effectively sell it doesn't make it unhappen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T15:30:45-07:00","id":1550672,"title":"","content":"I think the Hollow Ones have something of a bigger &quot;protagonist faction&quot; feel because of the fact the Traditions kind of got oversold in the early editions. It's hard to take them seriously as a bunch of people being hunted by the Union that controls the Consensus when they have these massive pocket dimensions where they rule their own kingdoms and have thousands of followers in their cults.<br /> <br /> Whereas the Hollow Ones are people who presumably have the solution to the Technocracy finding them as the Matrix's, &quot;Run.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T15:44:31-07:00","id":1550673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550656#post1550656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even while M20 made Orphans a more interesting option than they were before, I find it a hard sell to say they're <i>the</i> heroes, or protagonists, of the game. If anything, M20 made it easier to have <i><b>any</b></i> faction or option as a protagonist, but none is particularly better at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that prior to M20, the assumption was that an Orphan's options were extremely limited, that if you didn't belong to some faction or another, your Magickal practices had to consist of the equivalent of bubblegum and duct tape. M20 didn't put independent mages at the center of the game; but it <i>did </i>make it so that they're no longer out on the edges. <br /> <br /> And the factions were downgraded from &quot;this is what defines what your Magick is like&quot; to &quot;these are the mages you relate to the most&quot;. That is, they went from having metaphysical significance to &quot;merely&quot; social value. And with that change, it becomes possible to run a game where the protagonists can treat <i>\u200b\u200b\u200ball</i> factions as being different flavors of conformity, and where the only way to truly win the Ascension War is to do your own thing and not let <i>anyone </i>box you in. Which I think is kind of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> is going for in this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T04:10:19-07:00","id":1550681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550672#post1550672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Hollow Ones have something of a bigger &quot;protagonist faction&quot; feel because of the fact the Traditions kind of got oversold in the early editions. It's hard to take them seriously as a bunch of people being hunted by the Union that controls the Consensus when they have these massive pocket dimensions where they rule their own kingdoms and have thousands of followers in their cults.<br /> Whereas the Hollow Ones are people who presumably have the solution to the Technocracy finding them as the Matrix's, &quot;Run.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, <i>The Matrix</i> had Zion as a safe place to run to. Now, as we find out, it's not actually safe, but then neither are the chantries. Like, the Technocracy <i>are</i> coming for them. Plus, it's not exactly subtle that the big realms are run by some extremely dodgy people.<br /> <br /> On the other side, I'm not sure <i>Outcasts</i> really sells that. Like, they're quite blas\u00e9 about the possibility of being murdered by the Technocracy (to be fair, they <i>are</i> talking to a double-agent, but still, it's a setting book first, not a story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:31:00-07:00","id":1550694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550525#post1550525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take the view the Hollow Ones are the people who understand that beliefs don't have to be contradictory or that killing over them makes them more valid. If science and magic can be combined by a Hollow One doing a spell on a labtop or using pencillian with your magic potion then what ARE the Traditions and Union fighting over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being allowed to let your Freak Flag Fly Vs being told to sit down, shut up and go with the flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T10:33:12-07:00","id":1551001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550673#post1550673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And with that change, it becomes possible to run a game where the protagonists can treat <i>\u200b\u200ball</i> factions as being different flavors of conformity, and where the only way to truly win the Ascension War is to do your own thing and not let <i>anyone </i>box you in. Which I think is kind of what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> is going for in this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being possible to run such a game is different from such a game being the intended default for the setting.<br /> <br /> I agree that M20 made it possible to run this sort of game. I agree that you can make the Hollow Ones the protagonists of your chronicle, or <i>your version</i> of the setting.<br /> <br /> What I don't agree is that they've ever been intended as the protagonists of the setting as a whole, in the sense the Anarchs were meant as the protagonists of Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T11:46:15-07:00","id":1551003,"title":"","content":"Two things undermined any kind of mass popularity of the Hollow Ones over any of the Traditions. <br /> <br /> First, most players were not in fact Goths or wanted to play one. It was a particular musical sub-culture that had limited appeal, the popularity of the Cure not withstanding. Those players who did have an interest in that were often Goths themselves, and they usually wanted to roleplay something different.<br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions were simply much more interesting with some intellectual rigor behind them. They had fully thought out paradigms with extensive history and lore, and a distinctive type of enlightenment. In contrast, the Hollow Ones seemed weak, stunted, and limited. They lacked the &quot;wow, that's so cool; that's what I want to be&quot; compared to characters who knew super-kung fu, masters of Western hermeticism, spirit talking shamans, bad ass witches, mad scientists from the pulps, and so on. If those are the other members of your chantry, who wants to play the social misfit who listens to Bauhaus and Siouxsie Sioux while conducting a seance? That's a totally valid concept and could still be fun, but often seems lame compared to the alternatives for most people. Such characters could make interesting NPCs, but they usually lacked the appeal for people seeking to live out their power fantasies vicariously through their characters.<br /> <br /> Anarchs in Vampire are not analogous to Hollow Ones in Mage. The anarchs weren't actually a clan despite the Brujah being associated with them. Any character concept might find itself directed towards the anarch camp if she runs afoul of the prince. It's just a camp your character might fall into even if you aren't sympathetic to them. The Hollow Ones were just another splat who would already be on the same team as the Traditions except that they're so clueless and unimportant they often don't realize there are even people like the Marauders, Technocracy, or Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-13T13:12:51-07:00","id":1551005,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of their Underground Railroad. A safety network for weirdos it's both very playable and very on topic with Mage. Too bad they never did anything interesting with it.<br /> <br /> The Traditions never needed it because they're already organized as a protection network, that has vastly more resources than them to help each other. <br /> <br /> If the Disparate Alliance wasn't so ... well, let's say so willing to work together (to the point of accepting judgement from judges of other Crafts). Then such a concept could be useful to allow them a semblance of organization. You could have things like Disparate that are practically enemies sharing resorces within a neutral network that doesn't need to disclose where those come from, or traveling trough hostile territory to help kill a Nephandi, that everyone accepts it's a good thing enough to look the other way but not enough to want to directly interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2025, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T19:22:51-07:00","id":1551034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551003#post1551003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things undermined any kind of mass popularity of the Hollow Ones over any of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> First, most players were not in fact Goths or wanted to play one. It was a particular musical sub-culture that had limited appeal, the popularity of the Cure not withstanding. Those players who did have an interest in that were often Goths themselves, and they usually wanted to roleplay something different.<br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions were simply much more interesting with some intellectual rigor behind them. They had fully thought out paradigms with extensive history and lore, and a distinctive type of enlightenment. In contrast, the Hollow Ones seemed weak, stunted, and limited. They lacked the &quot;wow, that's so cool; that's what I want to be&quot; compared to characters who knew super-kung fu, masters of Western hermeticism, spirit talking shamans, bad ass witches, mad scientists from the pulps, and so on. If those are the other members of your chantry, who wants to play the social misfit who listens to Bauhaus and Siouxsie Sioux while conducting a seance? That's a totally valid concept and could still be fun, but often seems lame compared to the alternatives for most people. Such characters could make interesting NPCs, but they usually lacked the appeal for people seeking to live out their power fantasies vicariously through their characters.<br /> <br /> Anarchs in Vampire are not analogous to Hollow Ones in Mage. The anarchs weren't actually a clan despite the Brujah being associated with them. Any character concept might find itself directed towards the anarch camp if she runs afoul of the prince. It's just a camp your character might fall into even if you aren't sympathetic to them. The Hollow Ones were just another splat who would already be on the same team as the Traditions except that they're so clueless and unimportant they often don't realize there are even people like the Marauders, Technocracy, or Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that the Traditions had more depth than the Hollow Ones, but all things considered, that was not a high bar to clear. The material with the Traditions themselves was sorely lacking; even back in 2e when they had more occultists on the writer's team, the ideologies and cultures of the Traditions all felt very shallow. Conceptually, it just made no sense that you had to belong to a faction with a globe-spanning culture in order to have your character use some of the most common magical traditions on the planet. If anything I think that the organizations in Mage should have been based on political or practical aims rather than philosophical ones. I would argue that the Traditions may have actually stunted the imagination of some of the newer players, since they provided an easy paradigm package that didn't require much thought. Ideally, if someone is coming into a Mage game they should really be invested in coming up with the paradigm and magical style of their character, and that isn't needed if they can pick the menu for the core archetypes. The Traditions felt too archetypal to really be useful outside of the utility of an aid for beginners.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the Traditions' philosophical depth and lack thereof, I would also like to point out that the Traditions were always more about what media image for your wizard that you wanted. The Order of Hermes are plainly Ars Magicka wizards that don't even have much hermetic philosophy to them so much as trappings (to be fair, many magicians in Europe could not really be described as hermetic either; western ceremonial magic was never solely hermetic). Verbena are druids and also the Wicca player option. Sons of Ether are literally mad scientists (in reality, a lot of the theories of technomancers should be wildly different from one another, it's sort of handwaved in Ascension by stating that the Ether can also represent other hidden variables, but not a lot of effort was put into that). The Akashic Brotherhood are basically 90s kung-fu movie monks who rely more on the Southeast Asia trappings than the lore of sramanic traditions. The Cult of Ecstasy are the psychonaut faction (and I actually think that they were actually pulled off pretty decently compared to some of the other Traditions; it is hard to articulate why, but I think it has to do with how their ancient roots are often glossed over and the more recent spiritual movements of the 1960s onwards get more attention in their write-up, in a weird situation where being broad and generic was actually a benefit). The Celestial Chorus has the unlikely unitarian alliance and general early 1900s monistic theology going on (I have heard some people use the term Theosophy to describe them, but to be honest, they were always quite distinct from that movement). Euthanatoi don't really feel Vedantist in any of their incarnations, honestly. And I don't think much more needs to be said about the Dreamspeakers; needless to say, it is more than a bit funny to imagine that all shamanistic systems on the planet decided that they agreed on anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T09:25:13-07:00","id":1551070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551001#post1551001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being possible to run such a game is different from such a game being the intended default for the setting.<br /> <br /> I agree that M20 made it possible to run this sort of game. I agree that you can make the Hollow Ones the protagonists of your chronicle, or <i>your version</i> of the setting.<br /> <br /> What I don't agree is that they've ever been intended as the protagonists of the setting as a whole, in the sense the Anarchs were meant as the protagonists of Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that the idea that M20 is somehow <i>less </i>suitable than earlier editions to the sort of gameplay CTPhipps is advocating for is backwards. And as I said, the hypothetical new edition that Brucato outlined in <b>Mage Made Easy</b> would have embraced the independent mage as the intended protagonists of the setting; but in doing so, it would have rejected the idea of the Hollow Ones being the intended protagonists. <br /> <br /> Because each edition has moved the Hollow Ones further from being &quot;the faction of Orphans&quot;. 1e treated them as synonymous. 2e treated the Hollowers as a proto-Tradition composed of former Orphans looking for acceptance among the Traditions, and presented Orphans as a separate category. MRev presented the Hollow Ones as a Tradition featuring Romance as one of its defining features. Finally, M20 presented the Hollow Ones as a full-on Craft, complete with its own preferred Focus, with the Practices of Chaos Magick and Gutter Magick being &quot;near-universal among Hollow Ones.&quot; By contrast, M20's entry for Orphans emphasizes the <i>lack</i> of any unifying theme: even Gutter Magick, while mentioned, is merely &quot;especially prevalent in the technological world&quot; as opposed to being &quot;near-universal&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T10:23:28-07:00","id":1551073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551070#post1551070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is that the idea that M20 is somehow <i>less </i>suitable than earlier editions to the sort of gameplay CTPhipps is advocating for is backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone said that? I said that? True question, I don't remember anymore.<br /> <br /> But no, I actually agree with you. I'd say M20 didn't <i>particularly</i> emphasizes this kind of gameplay (either Hollow Ones or Orphans) because it embraced <i>all kinds</i> of gameplay. Which is in a sense de-emphasizing the traditional Traditions game (pun intended), I just find this wording misleading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T12:37:20-07:00","id":1551078,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone will really disagree that the agnostic approach of M20 that avoided defining any of the major factions as the primary protagonists was the best option possible for the edition, it seems like the question is revolving more around the conflation of Hollow Ones with Orphans and the utility of the Tradition/Craft/Convention paradigm as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T13:58:40-07:00","id":1551082,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Hollow Ones aren't useful in the game. They're one of my favorite Traditions. I don't think they work so well as a Craft, but that's not here or there.<br /> <br /> They're just not protagonist material. They work fine as one more faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T14:05:10-07:00","id":1551086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550525#post1550525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take the view the Hollow Ones are the people who understand that beliefs don't have to be contradictory or that killing over them makes them more valid. If science and magic can be combined by a Hollow One doing a spell on a labtop or using pencillian with your magic potion then what ARE the Traditions and Union fighting over?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well, there's no question of magic and science being opposed. Only the technocracy makes that distinction. <br /> <br /> Hollow ones didn't make anything new, doing a spell on a laptop? The virtual adepts call dibs. <br /> Penicillin with magic potion? The etherite did that as soon as they left the union<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T15:58:27-07:00","id":1551089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551086#post1551086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well, there's no question of magic and science being opposed. Only the technocracy makes that distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once one side starts a war, it's a war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hollow ones didn't make anything new, doing a spell on a laptop? The virtual adepts call dibs.<br /> Penicillin with magic potion? The etherite did that as soon as they left the union<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Virtual Adepts merge magic and computers. Just do super computers.<br /> <br /> Same for the SOE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T22:13:37-07:00","id":1551094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551089#post1551089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the Virtual Adepts merge magic and computers. Just do super computers.<br /> <br /> Same for the SOE.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't join the Traditions without absorbing a lot of their mysticism. Either as a requisite or a side effect, they accepted this, and you can be sure that a lot of their current members ascribe wholeheartedly to techgnosticism and other forms of mysticism with scientific trappings. Also, myriad members of the other Traditions did incorporate technology in their Magic.<br /> <br /> Everything the Hollow Ones do mixing tech and magic, others did before, both other Traditions and other Orphans.<br /> <br /> The Hollow Ones have their own thing going on, but <i><b>this</b></i> thing, it simply isn't particularly theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-16T22:51:55-07:00","id":1551095,"title":"","content":"The Virtual Adepts absolutely <i>do </i>merge Magick and computers. Not quite in the same way that House Verditius does, mind you; but to the VA, <i>numbers and mathematics are inherently magical. </i>Computers are &quot;merely&quot; a means of crunching numbers, something that low-rank VAs lean on because they haven't yet mastered the trick of crunching those numbers in their own head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T04:46:51-07:00","id":1551096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551089#post1551089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once one side starts a war, it's a war.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, it's not a war of science vs magic. It's a war of technocracy against magic (or really, against anything not technocratie). <br /> <br /> They may frame it as science vs magic, but it is merely their propaganda, as shown by the fact Thzt their very ennemies use both. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551089#post1551089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Virtual Adepts merge magic and computers. Just do super computers.<br /> <br /> Same for the SOE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They do both. The VA, especially in M20 mixe a heavy dose of mysticism in their practices, ans the Sons will use everything in their scientific models","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-17T11:57:32-07:00","id":1551102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551082#post1551082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're just not protagonist material. They work fine as one more faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it less that they aren't protagonist material than that the Traditions are protagonist material for a far wider group of people. I basically share much of how you see the Hollow Ones, but I'm still certain that the folks first at White Wolf and later Onyx Path always meant the Hollow Ones to be the coolest kids. <br /> <br /> I think something similar happened with the Ahl-i-Batin. I think that we're supposed to see these guys as cool and noble champions of utopia. They normally came across as smug hypocrites to me. <br /> <br /> Although so much of this setting (the WoD) is wonderful, there are areas were authorial intention simply failed. Oh well 10% failure is a 90% glorious success is still kind of wonderful. And it remains wonderful even while the 10% failure is deeply irksome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-05T08:49:13-07:00","id":1551479,"title":"","content":"As time goes on, though, I've been finding the Traditions work less as protagonist material. I guess I should say, I find their side in the fight very good for protagonists, but the actual traditions tend to come with a lot of strange choices that don't work for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 07-02-2025, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T14:25:12-07:00","id":1551959,"title":"","content":"I'm not a betting man, but I would find a very safe bet to say that Mage 5th edition will go exactly this route, of making the Hollow Ones, the gutter mages that do not follow any particular traditions, are not scions of big organized legacies... WoD 5th edition has unraveled most big organizations into provincial enclaves, or taken them out of the player core of the game, turning them into allies, enemies or other npcs. It has been so with V5, it was strongly so with H5, and a tendency (not fully staked in W5). <br /> <br /> Besides, there has always been a terrible dissonance between the gameplay, ruleset and fiction (or even aesthetics) of Mage. Much is shown and spoken about a guerilla covert war, a survival for the magic and awesome power that a mage can attain to change the world. Raincoats, alleys and secret encounters in downtrodden bars... Tim Bradstreet style. That doesn't really happen if you are a studen of hogwart in a big worldwide millenium spanning organization with hundreds or thousands of members, that are coordinated with many others (the Traditions), making up many thousands strong. Full of facilities, artifacts and teachers that would have no reason to leave a mage hanging in ignorancy.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think they will shift to a punk Mage style game. Reduce the scope, leave only few members of the Traditions, making it feel like a dying culture with some few elders keeping it alive, like the Jedi after Order 66, or a any other group after cultural genocide. <br /> In the same manner, the Technocracy will still be a threat, but headed by some warlord-type of strong leaders, that are trying to take control of the Union. Which is in disarray for some new or old metaplot development. Agents are cuthroat and desperate in some way. <br /> <br /> <br /> That's my take. Mage in WoD for me has lost the mystique (thats more of an Awakening thing), so it is more a game about taking power to change the world. What better way to do that than from the absolute bottom, Mages can and will ascend, that is what their Magick can do. Not a scared and powerless civillian, but a potentially almighty mage, trailing their own path or taking up the mantle of the fallen Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-30T15:49:32-07:00","id":1551964,"title":"","content":"Mage the Ascension never had that <i>mystique</i>. It was not really the point. It's a game about absolute power and what you do with it, where mysticism is <i><b>by design</b></i> just window-dressing. It matters just as far as it informs your beliefs and preferences, but those are important because you have the power to make them happen.<br /> <br /> I do think you're right about M5, anyway. Unless White Wolf Reborn shifts gears drastically (possible, but unlikely), they'll go all in on Punk Mage, and then the Hollow Ones are prime candidates for new intended protagonists as suggested in the Opening Post. And the elements for doing so are already set in motion by the end of Revised (<i>Threat Null</i> and the aftermath of the Avatar Storm), so it may even look better from a continuity perspective than the current lines.<br /> <br /> And I won't blame them too much by now. While I dislike the 5th Edition, it's as valid a game as any, if there's people for whom this game will click, all the better. I do think that the best path forward, if one day the IP comes to better management, is to split WoD in two and keep both versions as equally valid. (I won't stop pointing out bad writing, though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T13:32:55-07:00","id":1552041,"title":"","content":"As a diet goth I should be sympathetic but, I think the problem is simular to the anarchs with this idea. The hollow ones in wod have the aesthetic of a protagonist but they lack the depth required to carry the game. This is a major issue in vtm 5th but a critical one if you're going to try it with mage where it's really important to have some more than &quot;keeping it real on the streets.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again I can conceivable see 5th going through with either them or the orphans without doing a major re-design, it'll be bad writing but that hasnt stopped them so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-04T03:51:53-07:00","id":1552054,"title":"","content":"It's really like that for all the groups, but the others are linked in to archetypes or movements that have depth. The Hollow Ones were linked to a cultural moment that didn't last. Yes, there are still goths out there, but the Goth moment that the Hollow Ones link to is as gone and over as the Beats. Worse, the Hollow Ones are to that Goth moment as the term &quot;beatnik&quot; was to real Beats. <br /> <br /> No one who was an actual Beat called themselves a beatnik, except as a sarcastic joke. In many ways the Hollow Ones were always like a sitcom in 1970 seting an episode at a &quot;beanik hangout.&quot; A faded reflection of something poorly understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-05T22:47:53-07:00","id":1552094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1551964#post1551964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage the Ascension never had that <i>mystique</i>. It was not really the point. It's a game about absolute power and what you do with it, where mysticism is <i><b>by design</b></i> just window-dressing. It matters just as far as it informs your beliefs and preferences, but those are important because you have the power to make them happen.<br /> <br /> I do think you're right about M5, anyway. Unless White Wolf Reborn shifts gears drastically (possible, but unlikely), they'll go all in on Punk Mage, and then the Hollow Ones are prime candidates for new intended protagonists as suggested in the Opening Post. And the elements for doing so are already set in motion by the end of Revised (<i>Threat Null</i> and the aftermath of the Avatar Storm), so it may even look better from a continuity perspective than the current lines.<br /> <br /> And I won't blame them too much by now. While I dislike the 5th Edition, it's as valid a game as any, if there's people for whom this game will click, all the better. I do think that the best path forward, if one day the IP comes to better management, is to split WoD in two and keep both versions as equally valid. (I won't stop pointing out bad writing, though).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that was ABSOLUTELY what Revised was about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T09:57:48-07:00","id":1552105,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if <i>Revised</i> could be said to be about being <b>Punk</b>, specifically, at least not enough to make the <b>Hollow Ones</b> into protagonists back then, but it surely approaches, <b>in Mage</b>, the effect they've been going for in WoD5.<br /> <br /> Regardless if it was the intent or not, they can make M5 in their new style with the plot being just a continuation of <i>Revised</i>, that's beyond any doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-10T11:13:59-07:00","id":1552267,"title":"","content":"Im also weary about using 'punk' to justify writing decisions, especially controversial ones. Revised got a lot of blowback for v5 style &quot;were gonna use metaplot and mechanics to force you to play how we think you should.&quot; As I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-11T06:41:28-07:00","id":1552278,"title":"","content":"Yes, <i>Revised</i> had a lot of controversy because of this (despite having clearly superior rules compared to 2nd Ed in general), and doubly so in Mage, where it made the game far grittier than its proposal.<br /> <br /> But regardless of opinion on the writing decisions, WoD5 actively justifies itself on being punk, in style if not in spirit (I think in spirit they miss the point completely). It's problem with W5 is greatly because &quot;Legacy&quot; WtA isn't punk. HtR neither.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T17:18:34-07:00","id":1552570,"title":"","content":"Technically, all mages start out as an orphan or a Hollow-One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-21T17:52:20-07:00","id":1552572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1552570#post1552570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, all mages start out as an orphan or a Hollow-One.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there are Mages who belong to a Tradition, Convention or Craft right out of the bat.<br /> <br /> Mages of all stripes have Sleeper followers, like the Union's Extraordinary Citizens. The rate of Awakenings among those people are higher than usual. This person is already indoctrinated into the group and its Paradigm, and usually already a formal member, even if in a lesser position (that depends on the group).<br /> <br /> Granted, both the number of such followers and the frequency of Awakenings among them are up for the ST to decide, and it can go wildly in any direction, so they're not necessarily a big number of Mages. But they do exist. And it may be high enough for actually most Mages to come from such situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T01:41:50-07:00","id":1552580,"title":"","content":"Also, Hollow Ones are a Craft; and mages are no more likely to &quot;start out as&quot; a Hollow One than a Hermetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T04:53:05-07:00","id":1552582,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This would be a departure from the direction of WoD5e. The identities of the clans and tribes, may be changed or vague, but they are promoted as a defining feature of one's player character. They didn't come up with a list of verbs to characterise each tribe only to push Forsworn as the default.<br /> <br /> The changes to V5 and W5 mostly open up x-splats so that any character of the player's choosing can be included, provided that it's a character concept that fits the mores of the given playable society. For example, Tremere don't have to be in the pyramid and Black Furies don't have to be women (or metis men) or even particularly feminist.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if the<i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> institutions </span></i>of the Traditions and maybe Technocracy broke down. But the new player will still be presented with a set of Traditions, possibly alongside what we call Conventions. You wouldn't need the Hollow Ones to play a scrappy, free punk because you'd be able to play a scrappy, free punk hermetic, progenitor or kahuna. But not necessarily in the same historic, defined subcultures of NPCs in the existing versions of Mage.<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones will only be the main protagonists in M5 if pretty much all relevant mages, outside radical NPC factions, are Hollow Ones in practice and not in name.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T05:00:09-07:00","id":1552583,"title":"","content":"Indeed. As much as their Paradigm is a refusal to dwell on a unified magic theory, it's a specific Paradigm nonetheless. They've never been intended as just a &quot;non-Tradition&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T09:18:39-07:00","id":1552588,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's 100% fair. Early Mage frequently described the Hollowers as essentially a group of like-minded Orphans that grouped together for safety more than a group with a shared Paradigm. That was rather gone by late 2e, but it was part of their characterization (probably at its height in Outcasts, where Hollowers are considered on par with Caitiff and Ronin in terms of playable groups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T09:29:55-07:00","id":1552589,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I stand corrected. They weren't exactly a Craft/Tradition at first.<br /> <br /> But they were still an organized enough group that it seems strange to say a Mage would start out as a Hollow One. In fact, they may be the least likely group for a Mage to start at.<br /> <br /> The end result was still quite similar to a Craft, as far as organization goes, anyway, even if without a Paradigm, and they were the strangest addition to Outcasts (seriously, it should have used unaligned Orphans, with focus on those who can't make heads or tails of the Ascension War, yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T11:33:21-07:00","id":1552592,"title":"","content":"I think some of it is a time and place thing. In the 90s in the US, there was a distinct subculture of &quot;pop&quot; paganism and witchcraft. There was just enough books, magazines, and so on out there to cobble together an idea of a synthesis of Western occult traditions that was cohesive across large parts of the US such that you could have shared conversations about it with people from wildly different areas and backgrounds. The film <i>The Craft</i> came out at about the same time as Outcasts did, and it's about four girls that pick up witchcraft from some library books and a visit to a new age shop (run by basically a Verbena who fails in her initial attempt to recruit them to teach them a more measured approach). While ultimately you could argue the film feels more like &quot;Hollowers bad, join a real Tradition,&quot; the main characters are very Hollower-ish for most of the film. And as someone growing up in the US adjacent to plenty of people in on the neo-pagan subculture of the time... it felt like that could happen in Mage's setting in the 90s. The idea of stumbling your way into being a Hollower wasn't so far fetched.<br /> <br /> In 2025? Not really. Those in it for the rebel-fad have moved on, and those serious about it have developed far more detailed spiritual systems that has led to much more fragmentation as people have sought out to connect to less artificial occult practices (most of those people would be much more likely to resonate with the Verbena than the Hollowers... kinda like the movie predicted) than a bunch of teenagers finding the same small sets of books and writings sitting around in small bookstores (also something that's not really a thing in the US much either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T16:54:33-07:00","id":1552598,"title":"","content":"While I can't say I know much of the phenomena, I'm generally aware of that.<br /> <br /> But for the purpose of how Mage works, and taking this movie as an example, it looks to me more like a group of Orphans that resonates with the Hollow Ones, and would be prime material for their &quot;recruitment&quot; (AKA hang around until they're recognized as members as far as it goes), than <i>actual</i> Hollow Ones.<br /> <br /> After all, a similar situation could happen with any other group. All Traditions, Crafts and Conventions are heavily based on ideas and cultural trappings that exist outside the groups. Someone could start out resonating a lot with the Hermetics, the Choristers, or the Dream Speakers, nearing their ideas and Paradigms, without having any real connection with standing members of those Traditions. A member of an ethnic minority could feel the pull to the traditions and magic of their people outside the direct influence of the respective Craft, and so on.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally call those people members of the respective group, however similar they already are, because at the end of the day this is about affiliation, not belief (despite how important belief is in the matter, especially back then).<br /> <br /> Outcasts adds the problem that it is, in theory, about characters that have no access to the main social support networks of their splats. They're cut off from any established group that can offer them the benefits a typical member can take for granted, they have trouble even with basic interactions (give or take local nuance and how worse Ronins have it), and even with basic information, being the more likely to be ignorant about basic aspects of their condition and/or what's going on.<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones may be underdogs in Mage society, but they're not that screwed up. They're in the know and they have the same access to basic instruction as anyone else. They know the jargon, the people, what's at stake. And it isn't as if Mage didn't have a better example of an Outcast. It has, actual Orphans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-22T20:52:04-07:00","id":1552604,"title":"","content":"I largely don't disagree with you on this, I'm just highlighting that the books are inconsistent and there was a significant part of Mage's history-as-a-game where the difference between &quot;Orphan&quot; and &quot;Hollower&quot; was just having a social circle; where the Hollowers weren't even a real Craft that has support networks or instructions to offer and was more of a label than a functional group. I think the books moved away from that for good reasons, and I like the later Hollow Ones better as they're a more coherent element of the setting. But I do get the mindset that made them something less logical as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T05:52:30-07:00","id":1552607,"title":"","content":"In 1e, &quot;Orphan&quot; and &quot;Hollow One&quot; were synonymous. Outcasts was in the 1e era. 2e made the two distinct, though it still presented Hollowers as something that could easily be mistaken for Orphans if you weren't careful. MRev <i>really </i>leaned into defining what the Hollow Ones are, to the point that they got their own Tradition Book. <br /> <br /> And then, as I've mentioned before, M20 redefined the Orphans so that the old stereotype of Orphans as makeshift mages was no longer true. In M20, an Orphan is merely a mage who hasn't aligned with any faction; she <i>can</i> have a Focus every bit as detailed as the most OCD Hermetic would have. And the key phrase that I'd use for the M20 Orphans would be &quot;diversity of views.&quot; This is very distinct from the M20 Hollow Ones, who deliberately embrace a very specific approach to Magick: a blend of Chaos Magick and Gutter Magick. <br /> <br /> I <i>could </i>see M5 defaulting to M20's Orphans; because again, their defining trait is a lack of membership in a group. A setting where the Council of Nine is gone and the Traditions have fallen apart and everyone identifies with approaches to Magick such as &quot;devotee&quot; or &quot;magus&quot; or &quot;witch&quot; instead of institutions still strikes me as viable. I <i>can't </i>see M5 defaulting to the Hollow Ones. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T09:17:22-07:00","id":1552612,"title":"","content":"Outcasts is a 2e book despite the heavy 1e influence (and the book isn't really unclear about that, it's purposefully skewed to make the groups more viable as PCs and many of them were being downplayed by 2e even as Hollowers were actually getting scaled up in playability).<br /> <br /> That said, Orphans have always been presented as having formed paradigms (since they weren't called Focuses yet). What early 2e focused on in Initiates of the Art is the type of reasoning (deductive, inductive, and abductive) as what separates formally trained mages, Hollowers, and Orphans, rather than the paradigm/Focus itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T11:09:55-07:00","id":1552615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1552607#post1552607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>could </i>see M5 defaulting to M20's Orphans; because again, their defining trait is a lack of membership in a group. A setting where the Council of Nine is gone and the Traditions have fallen apart and everyone identifies with approaches to Magick such as &quot;devotee&quot; or &quot;magus&quot; or &quot;witch&quot; instead of institutions still strikes me as viable. I <i>can't </i>see M5 defaulting to the Hollow Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah i think this is the angle they'll go for. Its very bland but also safe. No way would they have the stones to have the Hollow Ones as the main guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> &gt;(.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T22:11:09-07:00","id":1552627,"title":"","content":"I don't know, Orphans are simply on their own, while Hollow Ones are positively counterculture to Mage society at large, and they have a clear preference for this take (however much you agree with their take on counterculture).<br /> <br /> They didn't made the Caitiff the standard for Vampire, instead they used the Anarchs (if not successfully). They made Hunters actively antagonistic to established groups, and their Garou aren't Ronins, either, but instead are pressed to be anti-elder where possible (if by seeing elders as idiots).<br /> <br /> While I think they'll probably butcher the concept of the Hollow Ones and make a very bland version of them, I do think they'll keep to them instead of focusing on Orphans. Or at least will make Orphans that are Hollow One knockoffs instead of actual Orphans as we understand them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T07:51:12-07:00","id":1552745,"title":"","content":"The books tended to make Orphans to be the default but the truth is most mages are people picked by a existing mage and led through Awakening.<br /> <br /> As for Punk.<br /> <br /> The problem with V5 was the fact that a lot of it didn't feel particularly punching up and everyone was afraid of crypto-fascism in Geek Media. Which...fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T22:25:43-07:00","id":1552758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1552745#post1552745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books tended to make Orphans to be the default but the truth is most mages are people picked by a existing mage and led through Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true, Mage isn't really consistent in this depiction.<br /> <br /> Some books heavily imply the vast majority start out under tutelage of other Mages, others heavily imply the opposite. Sometimes, especially the cores, the same book does both in different sections.<br /> <br /> It isn't even the only thing about Mage society that's inconsistent, in the end it's up to the Storyteller, but both extremes and anything in between is fully supported by the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1552745#post1552745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Punk.<br /> <br /> The problem with V5 was the fact that a lot of it didn't feel particularly punching up and everyone was afraid of crypto-fascism in Geek Media. Which...fair enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I think the miss the point about Punk in spirit. Or at least it's one of the reasons.<br /> <br /> But however wrong they are about their idea of Punk, <b>it's still their intent</b>. It is, or tries to be, Punk in style and aesthetics, and in whatever they think Punk to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T05:39:15-07:00","id":1552767,"title":"","content":"Punk Rock came and went so quickly. Deborah Harry of <b>Blondie</b> took everything interesting and distinctive about punk into the pop mainstream before the <b>Sex Pistols </b>were really a band. The &quot;documentary&quot; <b>The Great Rock and Roll Swindle </b>makes it clear, punk was mainly posturing and sham even if there was a serious core. <br /> <br /> Since the 1970s (I'll be 65 this October) the term &quot;Punk&quot; has been wildly overused to mean <i>edgy and relevant.</i> Thanks to Cyberpunk, Steampunk, and a dozen other similar terms of increasing obscurity, punk also means a genre mainly defined by style and attitude. <br /> <br /> All of this makes defining and discussing intelligently the meaning of <b><i>Gothpunk</i></b> orders of magnitude harder than nailing jello to the wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T18:27:21-07:00","id":1552785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1552767#post1552767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Punk Rock came and went so quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you look at their influence in pop music. Most of punk stayed underground, so it has little visibility outside the punk scene.<br /> <br /> But more important than the Punk-Rock music genre is the Punk movement, and within it the Punk Literature.<br /> <br /> While not everything that slams &quot;Punk&quot; to the name is more than aesthetics, some, like Cyberpunk, are complex sub-genres.<br /> <br /> Gothic-Punk isn't the most brilliant exemple, and a lot of it is aesthetics, but there's a lot of real influence from both Punk and Gothic Literature, especially on 1st edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-05T23:04:31-07:00","id":1552945,"title":"","content":"Eh, punk is an outgrowth of the fact that rock and rock's own inspirations were rebellious. It always gets co-opted but its an outgrowth of a much larger trend in music.<br /> <br /> Whenever there is song, there is counter culture ranging from &quot;Eve of Destruction&quot; to &quot;War Pigs&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T15:00:13-08:00","id":1557385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1550523#post1550523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, but I don't get in any edition any reason for the Hollow Ones to be the protagonists.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see it from a thematic standpoint.<br /> <br /> Awakening presents the idea of True Magic as reality being dictated by your perception of it.<br /> <br /> For the Hollow Ones, who effectively make up their own approach to magic, with none of the codified traditions weighing them down, they would actually make for a very appropriate choice of protagonist. Encouraging the player to build their own paradigms, instead of following in someone else's footsteps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T03:15:27-08:00","id":1557585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1557385#post1557385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Hollow Ones, who effectively make up their own approach to magic, with none of the codified traditions weighing them down, they would actually make for a very appropriate choice of protagonist. Encouraging the player to build their own paradigms, instead of following in someone else's footsteps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not the Hollow Ones, that's an Orphan.<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones do have a Paradigm-of-sorts: magic is anything that works. This is a very versatile thing, but from a Paradigm standpoint it's still a very specific belief, not &quot;building your own Paradigm&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T07:44:20-08:00","id":1557600,"title":"","content":"But I thought the whole premise of True Magic is that you have to believe in its ability to work, in order for it to actually do so.<br /> <br /> Thus <i>&quot;anything that works&quot; </i>can literally be <i>&quot;anything I want.&quot;</i> - It works, because I say it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T11:52:45-08:00","id":1557609,"title":"","content":"Here's what M20 says about the Focus of the Hollow Ones:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Focus:</b> Darklings use whatever they\u2019ve got to work with \u2013 typically things discarded by society. Broken toys, occult goodies, and symbols and behaviors that so-called respectable people shun make potent tools in the hands of a Hollow mage. Belief-wise, that hollow image is appropriately symbolic: these folks tend to see themselves as vessels of life and death, pouring their Arts out or carrying those cosmic forces from place to place. Magick, then, comes from the proper comprehension and intentional use of the energies that, in most people, are simply wasted. <i>Everything is Chaos, an Illusion, or a Mistake</i>, probably on a <i>One-Way Trip to Oblivion</i>. Some Hollowers insist that <i>It\u2019s All Good</i>, but they\u2019re the minority. <i>Chaos</i> and <i>gutter magick</i> are near-universal among the Hollow Ones. Although such Arts don\u2019t actually nurture chaos, they thrive in the chaos of our age.</span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the Focus for Orphans, for contrast:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Focus:</b> Orphans accept almost any worldview that provides a place for magickal powers. Some orphans become technomancers too, focusing their Arts through technological tools and beliefs. Religious creeds, transhumanist philosophy, occult dabbling, and ethnic practices provide the most common focuses for orphan magick, and popular culture that integrates several of them (often known as \u201cgutter magick\u201d or \u201chigh eclecticism\u201d) is especially prevalent in the technological world.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So Gutter Magick is mentioned for both, though it's &quot;near universal&quot; for Hollow Ones but only &quot;especially prevalent&quot; for Orphans. Also, the only other Practice mentioned for Hollow Ones is Chaos Magick, which is also nearly universal for them; for Orphans, <i>every Practice in the game</i> is a potential candidate. <i>This </i>is &quot;encouraging the player to build their own paradigms&quot;.<br /> <br /> So let's look at Chaos Magick and Gutter Magick, to get a sense of how Hollow One Magick works:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Chaos Magick </b><br /> It\u2019s not what you think it is. Although the term \u201cchaos magic\u201d tends to be associated with demons and evil, occultists understand chaos magick as a postmodern and often improvisational Art. Like other mystic practices, it emphasizes knowledge, reflection, and other forms of self-improvement. This revolutionary inversion of traditional mystic disciplines, however, depends upon personal intuition and interpretation; individual freedom; a deliberately iconoclastic approach; and an often subversive use of pop-culture symbols, social behaviors, and improvised designs.<br /> <br /> Chaos magick spits in the face of established dogma. Often regarded by outsiders as a Left-Hand Path, it\u2019s a sex, drugs, and rock-n-roll sort of practice, raising and directing personal energy (that is, Quintessence) through extreme experiences. Obviously, this sort of thing appeals to Cultists of Ecstasy, whose more formal practices \u2013 Tantra, vision questing, ordeals, and crazy wisdom (see below) \u2013 have been integrated into the chaos-magick potpourri. Even that diverse culture, however, is too confining for many chaos practitioners, whose embrace of the Chaosphere \u2013 the whirling fractal of absolute existence \u2013 resists confinement in any form.<br /> <br /> Playful yet serious, each chaos-magick practice draws from the individual practitioner\u2019s experiences and desires. Depending upon the individual practitioner, it can integrate formalized ritual or involve spontaneous improvisation\u2026 or both, or neither. Flexibility and personal investment are innate elements of the practice as a whole, often connected to psychic thought forms called egregores: concepts given reality through extensive investment of psychic energy. (See the Instruments entry for Thought Forms, pp. 598-599.) Some folks use toys and Tarot cards, whereas others draw sigils, craft graphic novels, run raves, stage flash mobs, and concoct elaborate pranks on society at large. Eris, Bob, the Flying Spaghetti Monster\u2026 these deities supplant the classic divinities in a chaotic pantheon whose figureheads are less concerned with worship than with inversion. Each mage, then, is a vortex of potential whose Will spins energy into being. And if this sounds too abstract to be useful, then you\u2019re thinking about it too hard.</span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rather than being &quot;build your own paradigm&quot;, this is more like &quot;make it up as you go, and don't try to frame a coherent picture of how it all works.&quot; And:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Gutter Magick</b><br /> The most practical magick practice is the one that uses whatever you\u2019ve got to work with. Sure, wizards and cyborgs and Enlightened tycoons can afford all the best ritual gear around. What happens, though, when you\u2019re more or less broke? Homeless, maybe? Living in a squat or stuck on the street or getting by as part of the working poor? Well then, you use gutter magick, the craft of making do.<br /> <br /> Composed of odds and ends with symbolic connotations, gutter magick features coins, cards, toys, scraps, bottles, cans, nails, junk, graffiti, and things crafted out of the cast-offs of consumer society. Dead TVs, old magazines, cardboard boxes, gnawed chicken bones, sacrificed rats and alley cats, old clothes repurposed and restyled with feral urban flair\u2026 such instruments direct the Will of the truly destitute. On the next rung up the socioeconomic ladder, lower-class mages use cheap tricks, cheesy clothes, New Age books, action figures, and other tokens of postmodern mall-magic. When invested with Awakened intentions, these otherwise useless trinkets provide focus for orphans, Hollowers, and other mystics with more ambition than resources.<br /> <br /> As with many other mystic practices, art forms a potent force in gutter magick. Hip-hop culture, Gothic rock, the various flavors of heavy metal, the blues, neotribal, techno-industrial, and even country/ western music styles provide soundtracks for the mystic side of the urban scene. Inside the clubs, dancing and drugs create hypnotic atmospheres in which it often seems like anything could happen. A paranormal survival tactic, gutter magick skulks in the shadows of the alley between respectability and forbidden Arts. Gutter magick proves that you don\u2019t need high wizardry and ancient tomes in order to get attention (if not necessarily respect) from the spirit world. In its darker elements, such magick employs guns, blades, cheap sex and cheaper booze, crimes and punishments, madness and desperation. Though not exactly new in form, it\u2019s a common practice in the new millennium.</div> <br /> <br /> So Gutter Magick is about using whatever is on hand to work magick, even \u2014 no, <i>especially </i>\u2014 if it's cobbled together. Put these together, and the Hollow Ones' magick is about making it up as you go: less a matter of developing your own paradigm, it's as close to <i>rejecting </i>having a Focus as you're ever going to get.<br /> <br /> By contrast, an Orphan could be just like a member of any given Tradition, Craft, or Convention, save only for the lack of membership. \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-17-2026, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T19:51:50-08:00","id":1557628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1557609#post1557609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's what M20 says about the Focus of the Hollow Ones:</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for providing better clarification on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T13:08:58-08:00","id":1558365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1557585#post1557585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not the Hollow Ones, that's an Orphan.<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones do have a Paradigm-of-sorts: magic is anything that works. This is a very versatile thing, but from a Paradigm standpoint it's still a very specific belief, not &quot;building your own Paradigm&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong but aren't 99% of Hollow Ones Orphans? It was sort of their deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T13:18:07-08:00","id":1558366,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I think it was initially.<br /> <br /> But at least by <i>Outcasts</i> there does seem to be at least some kind of distinction. Like in the books narrative, there's Penny Dreadful and the Hollow Ones, and then there's the guy who runs the occult bookshop who's an Orphan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T14:42:01-08:00","id":1558368,"title":"","content":"It's often said that the Hollow Ones are a group of like minded Orphans. The various traditions take in Orphans as do many but not all Crafts. Some Orphans stay loners on a singular path. Most join some group of Mages or other Supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I could see an Orphan Mage joining with Changelings, certain Shifters, or hanging out with Wraiths or Risen. Some groups Sorcerers will have Mages in them even if they don't understand the Mage/Sorcerer dichotomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T06:14:16-07:00","id":1561989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1558365#post1558365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong but aren't 99% of Hollow Ones Orphans? It was sort of their deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that you in particular only likes Mage 1st Edition, yes.<br /> <br /> For anyone who prefers anything from Outcasts onwards, no. They're their own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1558368#post1558368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's often said that the Hollow Ones are a group of like minded Orphans. The various traditions take in Orphans as do many but not all Crafts. Some Orphans stay loners on a singular path. Most join some group of Mages or other Supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st Edition Hollow Ones were Orphans. After that they're effectively a Craft with close ties to the Traditions, although their description and reputation aren't flattering or consistent.<br /> <br /> Orphans are defined by lack of a faction that can explain what they are and give support in their life as a Mage, so while most factions do accept Orphans, that also by definition makes them stop being Orphans.<br /> <br /> That's their whole point since Outcasts: they're outside Mage society and ignorant of it. Other groups don't take their independence well and they have no support. When they understand anything at all about the Awakened it's spotty at best, and they're not on the grapevine. This is not what a Hollow One is. Orphans are like the Caitiff or Lost Cubs (not Ronin).<br /> <br /> You can have an Orphan that's a Kinfolk rite master that's particularly skillful. They know nothing about what they really are and won't ever see themselves as anything else. The only Mage of a group of self-made occultists, just thinking the group's theories are correct with no actual knowledge of the supernatural. If the Orphan manages to shape this group into more proper form, to the point they develop some Numina at least or a Sorcerous Path, you can say they started a Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T09:41:15-07:00","id":1561999,"title":"","content":"I always liked the Hollow Ones so much that I've always pretended they don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T15:20:59-07:00","id":1562012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1561989#post1561989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that you in particular only likes Mage 1st Edition, yes.<br /> <br /> For anyone who prefers anything from Outcasts onwards, no. They're their own thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Edition Hollow Ones were Orphans. After that they're effectively a Craft with close ties to the Traditions, although their description and reputation aren't flattering or consistent.<br /> <br /> Orphans are defined by lack of a faction that can explain what they are and give support in their life as a Mage, so while most factions do accept Orphans, that also by definition makes them stop being Orphans.<br /> <br /> That's their whole point since Outcasts: they're outside Mage society and ignorant of it. Other groups don't take their independence well and they have no support. When they understand anything at all about the Awakened it's spotty at best, and they're not on the grapevine. This is not what a Hollow One is. Orphans are like the Caitiff or Lost Cubs (not Ronin).<br /> <br /> You can have an Orphan that's a Kinfolk rite master that's particularly skillful. They know nothing about what they really are and won't ever see themselves as anything else. The only Mage of a group of self-made occultists, just thinking the group's theories are correct with no actual knowledge of the supernatural. If the Orphan manages to shape this group into more proper form, to the point they develop some Numina at least or a Sorcerous Path, you can say they started a Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's the changing nature of mage but you're describing a different thing than Orphans as I remember them.<br /> <br /> You can be an Orphan Virtual Adept, Orphan Hollow One, or Orphan Celestial Choirster.<br /> <br /> Orphans are those who aren't recruited and awakened by a Tradition. They awaken spontaneously when they figure out the Ascension on their own.<br /> <br /> Which offends mages who had to be led through the mysteries like the Order of Hermes likes to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T22:44:45-07:00","id":1562028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1562012#post1562012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it's the changing nature of mage but you're describing a different thing than Orphans as I remember them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally what I meant.<br /> <br /> Orphans changed a long time ago. The book you used to open the thread started it and by mid 2nd edition there was no trace left of the 1st Edition meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T01:56:06-07:00","id":1562038,"title":"","content":"Okay, so at some point, Orphans became different from Awakening but now just means Rogue Mage.<br /> <br /> Gotcha.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, Outcasts is one of my favorite books and I never saw that as when it changed. Mind you, the Hollow Ones play a big role in that book and I prefer its take on them to the Hollow Ones Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T08:53:19-07:00","id":1562047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1562038#post1562038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weirdly, Outcasts is one of my favorite books and I never saw that as when it changed. Mind you, the Hollow Ones play a big role in that book and I prefer its take on them to the Hollow Ones Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it's as different as you think.<br /> <br /> The concept of Orphans changed because the whole notion of the Awakening being common in &quot;training grounds&quot; of many sort changed. By mid-2nd edition it's well established that this is a real but very small thing, and the Awakening is a mystery: no one knows how to provoke or predict it. And that means the bulk of Mages are post-Awakening recruits.<br /> <br /> Calling those Orphans would be pointless, so since then it's firmly established that Orphan is a Mage with no formal training by any group. Not exactly rogue, because leaving still makes you ex-something rather than Orphan, but they are defined by not having allegiances, yes.<br /> <br /> What happens to the Hollow Ones is... Not much, really. They're still the same group who chose to not join a Tradition/Convention and prefer to not impose their view on each other. Their culture is exactly that, culture rather than grand philosophy. But culture still shapes your Paradigm, so theirs is not derived from a theory of reality, but attitude towards it. Which frankly, gives you exactly the Hollow Ones of Outcasts.<br /> <br /> So the Revised Hollow Ones are counterculture Goths who have no formal organization, reject participation in formal factions and live at the margins of &quot;proper&quot; Mage society, but are kind of <u><i>tolerated</i></u> by the Traditions as annoying but still more hands against the Technocracy. Is that any different from Outcasts?<br /> <br /> Only reason they're not called Orphans anymore is that Orphan changed meaning, and the Hollow Ones didn't. As they have each other and a good notion of what's going on, for current terminology they fit Craft better, but it's just taxonomy.<br /> <br /> Sincerely, I think Revised Hollow + Orphans follow the spirit of Outcasts way more than 1st Edition versions. You should really stop being so attached to old terminology and know more about what Mage became after that (and still 30 years ago).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T18:05:57-07:00","id":1563025,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it. Given the inherent individuality of all Mages. Even the most carefully mentored Hermetic Apprentice is, in a deeper sense, an orphan in key ways. The transitions that matter are by necessity so individual you always have to go through alone. Having a good mentor and a tradition to fall back on helps with learning and internalizing the experience. But Awakening is alone, individual, and unique. Orphans are baked into the system. Traditions are creations were mages help each other along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T19:53:03-07:00","id":1563026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550508-i-always-felt-the-hollow-ones-should-have-been-the-protagonists-of-mage?p=1563025#post1563025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it. Given the inherent individuality of all Mages. Even the most carefully mentored Hermetic Apprentice is, in a deeper sense, an orphan in key ways. The transitions that matter are by necessity so individual you always have to go through alone. Having a good mentor and a tradition to fall back on helps with learning and internalizing the experience. But Awakening is alone, individual, and unique. Orphans are baked into the system. Traditions are creations were mages help each other along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why Orphans are better defined as not having a faction to back them up.<br /> <br /> If you follow the concepts to their conclusions, all Mages are unique, Factions don't change your Magic. You do.<br /> <br /> What set them apart, more than any other inner splat in the WoD, is just political affiliation and access to information.<br /> <br /> Hence an Orphan being better defined as just a Mage that has no such backing and must find out things the hard way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}